# SRG-APP-000755-AU-000140  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must implement an audit reduction capability that
# supports on-demand reporting requirements.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000755-AU-000140
group:           V-263560
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-003823
control_rev5:    AU-7

contribution:    The same search-time knowledge layer that reduces audit records feeds the
                 saved reports that satisfy a reporting requirement, and both the reduction
                 and the report that consumes it are set in application configuration.

governs:         macros.conf - Reusable fragments of search language.
governs:         props.conf - How incoming data is recognized, parsed and timestamped.
governs:         savedsearches.conf - Saved searches, scheduled reports and alerts.

check:           props.conf [<source type>] present
check:           macros.conf [<STANZA_NAME>] definition non_empty
check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] search non_empty
check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] enableSched equals 1
check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] cron_schedule non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] action.email.sendpdf https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/savedsearches.conf
vendor:          savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] search https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/savedsearches.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The reporting cycle, the recipients and the required report format are
                 organization-defined parameters recorded in the system security plan.
external:        Delivery of the rendered report rests on the mail transfer agent and on
                 network reachability from the Splunk host.
external:        The delivered form of a report, which is organization-defined and spread
                 across five savedsearches.conf switches and alert_actions.conf, so no
                 single key carries it.

citation:        props.conf.spec:80 [<spec>], :1085 REPORT-<class>, :1329 LOOKUP-<class>;
                 macros.conf.spec:52 definition; savedsearches.conf.spec:44 search, :73
                 enableSched = [0|1] default 0, :79 cron_schedule, :383
                 action.email.sendpdf = [1|0] default 0.
finding:         Assessed at the application layer alone: no knowledge layer is bound to
                 the audit source types in scope, or the report that consumes the reduction
                 is not dispatched on a stated cycle, so the application's audit reduction
                 does not support the reporting requirement.
